    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "AAAAW3///VQ\u003d",
        "filename": "doc/source/security_details.rst",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 157,
      "author": {
        "id": 9098
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-04-09T01:26:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My intention of \"configurable\" was so a deployer would be able to know if they can control the algorithm used for a particular purpose.  For example, someone may have a requirement that says md5 can\u0027t be used at all in their environment.  The \"configurable\" section is to let them know if they can do anything about it.  If there is a strong reason why it can\u0027t be configurable (like EC2 and S3 compatibility), it\u0027s important for us to call out so deployers understand why.\n\nIf we want to describe end-user facing vs. server side only, we should probably list that separately somehow.",
      "parentUuid": "AAAAWn//3TM\u003d",
      "revId": "b4accb6b9ff4fe6084d2d79016a22249ccc52862",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
