    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "AAAAW3///Ts\u003d",
        "filename": "doc/source/security_details.rst",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 235,
      "author": {
        "id": 9098
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-04-09T01:26:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we know that a particular backend is more secure, we should call that out.  It would hopefully be clear from the security options listed under each backend.\n\nFor each backend, it would be nice to explain how access to the backend is controlled (authentication and authorization) and how the data is protected (encryption and signing).  I was able to determine some of this above, but not all of it. Any help filling those details in would be great.  For example:\n\n- How is access to memcached controlled?  Is there any authentication, or do we just rely on local (or network) access?\n\n- Where are encryption/signing keys set for memcached?  How are they protected?\n\n- SQL details on authentication needs to be added (the \"connection\" setting in the \"[sql]\" section of keystone.conf).  Are there more secure authentication options that we can use other than putting a clear-text password in keystone.conf?\n\n- KVS has no details, as I wasn\u0027t sure of how to protect it.",
      "parentUuid": "AAAAWn//3ic\u003d",
      "revId": "b4accb6b9ff4fe6084d2d79016a22249ccc52862",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    }
